Regression for [temp.deduct.call]/4.3 derived-to-base template
argument deduction.  A function template taking
`Base<T> const volatile*` called with an argument of type
`Derived<bool> const volatile*` where `Derived<U> : Base<U>` must
deduce `T = bool` via the derived-to-base pointer rule.

This is the macOS libc++ `__cxx_atomic_load` failure pattern:
`__cxx_atomic_impl<_Tp>` publicly derives from
`__cxx_atomic_base_impl<_Tp>`; `__cxx_atomic_load` takes a pointer
to the base template, so calling it through a pointer to the
derived template needs this deduction rule.
